<title>USA: Peoples Home Savings up after market debut.</title>
<headline>Peoples Home Savings up after market debut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Shares of Peoples Home Savings Bank hit 13-1/2 on their first day of trading Thursday, up 35 percent from the bank's offering price of $10 a share.</p>
<p>The Beaver Falls, Pennsylvania bank sold 1.24 milion shares in a minority offering for gross proceeds of $12.42 million. The bank's new mutual holding company, PHSB Bancorp MHC, acquired 1.52 million shares or 55 percent of the outstanding shares of the company.</p>
<p>The bank had $205 million in assets as of March 31.</p>
